        {
          "text": "{\"a2uiMeta\":{\"note\":\"Here's London to Paris on Friday 20 November 2026, train against flight. The prices and times are illustrative demo values, not live fares or timetables. For city-centre to city-centre travel I'd recommend the Eurostar. Which would you like to take?\",\"ask\":{\"surfaceId\":\"ask-1\"}}}\n\nThe Eurostar runs from St Pancras to Gare du Nord in about 2h 20m, and once you allow for check-in it's roughly 3 hours door to door. A flight is quicker in the air at about 1h 15m, but airport transfers and security bring the full trip to around 4h 30m. The train is also the better choice if you want to avoid hold-baggage fees.",
